# Rename to `.env` to activate. Local to your machine - .env is gitignored.

# Develop against a sibling platform-pkg-dev checkout instead of the released one.
#
# `dev sync` normally fetches the latest platform-pkg-dev version from the host in
# platform-pkg-dev's versions.json. With this set it reads ../platform-pkg-dev/VERSION instead,
# so a local checkout is the source of truth and nothing hits the network.
#
# Note that if this package depends on platform-pkg-dev via `link:` or `file:`, sync
# never rewrites the dependency anyway - the local checkout is always current.
# This flag matters when the spec is a version but you want to compare against
# a checkout.
#
# IS_LOCAL_DEV=true

# --- CDK ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Read by cdk/bin/app.ts. The CDK CLI sets these itself from your AWS profile
# when you run `cdk deploy` or `cdk diff`, so you only need them here for a
# `cdk synth` that must resolve a real account - context lookups, or anything
# environment-specific.
#
# Leaving the account unset keeps the stack environment-agnostic: one
# synthesized template that deploys anywhere.
#
# CDK_DEFAULT_ACCOUNT=123456789012
# CDK_DEFAULT_REGION=eu-west-2
